    "udt_g357_g360_conditional_banking_2026-09-07/BANKING_RECORD.md": {
      "sha256": "34588fee0d20bbfb2de12dc2dc31d743e36f300af94bfe5ccb58595c2ac73a1a",
      "text": "# SC2--SC5 conditional mathematical banking record\n\nDate: 2026-09-07 UTC. Source/preservation baseline:\ned2f7432f068aa7a72628382b890596b3efba06a on synchronized grok.\n\n## Authority and disposition\n\nCharles explicitly authorizes banking SC2--SC5 as conditional mathematical\nresults at EXACTLY their reviewed scopes. G357=SC2, G358=SC3, G359=SC4,\nG360=SC5. SC1 remains a source map, with no new result row or grade.\nCommon disposition: BANKED_DERIVED_CONDITIONAL, VERIFIED-WITH-CAVEATS,\nOWNER_AUTHORIZED, NOT_PHYSICAL_ADOPTION, NOT_CANON. This record supplies the\nlater banking disposition; the original candidates/reviews retain their\nhistorical UNPROMOTED/pending wording without alteration.\n\nAll owner-provisional premises, supplied initial/query data, optional\nconditions, CHOSEN phase/product and curvature recipes remain explicit.\nNo physical identification, physical counting, detector law, recipe adoption,\nnew physical premise or canon follows. The physical identification remains OPEN.\nThe proposed persistence campaign awaits Charles; no new campaign is authorized.\n\nThis is promotion of already reviewed mathematics, not a fresh scientific\nconstruction. Completion of integration checks and fresh fidelity review is\nrecorded in EXECUTION_RECORD.md and its exact captures. A draft integration\nor a commit alone is not a passed gate.\n\n## Frozen evidence and dependencies\n\nThe entire source campaign is\n`udt_shared_readout_metric_constraint_campaign_2026-09-06/`, pinned at the\nbaseline above:442 tracked files,441 manifest payloads.\nARTIFACT_SHA256SUMS hash:\n32daf9c0b69ec4107b310f9275a6bc1e2b674f7c40fb456811f0f6d122a26cfe.\nIt includes original/repaired implementations, actual failures, source-first\nreview notes, direct reviews, focused repair review and closure evidence.\nNo source-campaign file is rewritten by this promotion.\n\nAccepted scientific inputs were pinned by that campaign at\n70034a6faa9264bf054eb473d5eb7a0889f3d2de. Exact source inventories remain\nstep_0N/SOURCE_SHA256SUMS. Later review/dependency additions retain their\nown frozen manifests. SC1 gates SC2--SC4 by source/type/domain mapping;\nSC5 depends on reviewed SC2. SC3 and SC4 do not depend on SC2's theorem.\nEarlier G353--G356 banking and its original campaign remain unchanged.\n\nG351's standard finite nonnegative countably additive label measure and\nsource-free conservation are owner-provisional. G352's clock-rate readout\nis owner-provisional and its continuous total-phase-variation, phase-\nindependent product is CHOSEN. Their use does not derive population.\nG312's quiet-GR/Local Metric Sufficiency premises provisionally control the\nbounded Einstein arena. W4 remains WORKING/POSIT; G261/G348 require actual\nsupplied smooth Lorentzian geometry. G321/G335 carry their imported local\ndevelopment theorem and bounded data limitations. These are not new premises.\n\nRemoving ONLY G357--G360 must recover the exact prior339-row registry hash\n23096ecbbdace34bb9f3add2cc288c9c62edd264a096620955be04b0510a7429.\nCurrent tracking becomes343 rows through G360; old339 rows stay byte-identical.\n\n## G357 \u2014 SC2-CONE, SC2-OVERLAP, SC2-INVISIBLE\n\nControlling scientific text: step_02/CANDIDATE_ARGUMENT.md, all sections.\nArgument SHA256:\n41bb97aa12ba9d8e30d34d73a324095103a54c520d154889a8b514c1f036b5cf.\nDirect review: step_02/review/PHASE_B_ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW.md, SHA256\n56c2450bacfdb63d2c9ef7cc2c12f9c70db1c3d318b758786664636caca84707.\nReview context /root/tri_step02_review; 0/1 repair cycles used.\n\nFor a finite partition into NONEMPTY measurable cells, fixed finite\nnonnegative simple kernels A, and an arbitrary finite nonnegative measure,\nideal records obey y=A M with M>=0. Conversely every nonnegative M is\nrealized by point-evaluation measures on labels, without requiring measurable\nsingletons. Thus y lies in the closed finite cone iff all separating dual\ninequalities h.y>=0 with A^T h>=0 hold. Zero rows/columns/measure are retained.\nThis is not a closure theorem for arbitrary nonconstant kernels or a claim\nthat every matrix is realizable on every fixed metric/query.\n\nWith exact shared windows P union Q, Q union R, P union R and fixed positive\nrates r_i, normalized records z_i=y_i/r_i have masses\n(p,q,r)=((z1+z3-z2),(z1+z2-z3),(z2+z3-z1))/2.\nFeasibility is exactly the three triangle inequalities; (1,1,3) fails.\nDisjoint windows instead allow every nonnegative record. The supplied\nMinkowski phase/observer construction supports this chosen protocol only.\nUnknown cell masses and finer measures are ordinary data, not selected laws.\n\nEqual records mean cell-mass differences lie in ker A, subject to positivity.\nInvertible overlap fixes cell masses, not within-cell content. Zero columns\nare invisible; no probability/total-mass normalization is hidden.\nLabel atoms are not atomic phase/time counting. No detector, noise, finite-\ntime integration, arbitrary kernel, physical content or PDE conclusion.\n\nAnalytic cone/separation/measure arguments bear the quantifiers. Author22\nguard groups and four actual mutant failures are regression. Source-first\nreview plus independent elimination/feasibility checked776 assertions,\n343 rational controls. That implementation was written after proof/summary\nexposure but before author code; source-first argument preceded proof.\nThe disjoint guard r*(z/r)==z is an arithmetic identity, not independent\nfeasibility proof. Representative window points do not prove full preimages;\nthe analytic set argument and independently checked construction supply them.\n\n## G358 \u2014 SC3-COMPATIBILITY, SC3-RECONSTRUCTION, SC3-BLINDNESS\n\nControlling text: step_03/CANDIDATE_ARGUMENT.md, all sections.\nArgument SHA256:\n1d9ec37b3c7cbec4c308ea2177a824077052a2b5541cb34e23e005730a21d903.\nDirect review: step_03/review/PHASE_B_ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW.md, SHA256\n04e88f334ac7f75fb0795790f6b3db813165ca4cd47fa6a359329b029a32a721.\nReview context /root/tri_step03_review; 0/1 repairs.\n\nAt one event in a supplied oriented orthonormal (-+++) frame,\nQ_abcd=g(R(e_a,e_b)e_c,e_d) with G348's stated curvature convention.\nRic_bc=sum_a eta_aa Q_abca. Supply unit future u, null k_i^+=u+e_i and\nk_i^-=u-e_i, prescribed affine scale at the event and cyclic screens.\nE_ij=Q_i00j and the six symmetric null-screen tide matrices give24\ndeclared coordinates. They are compatible with ONE algebraic Einstein\ncurvature tensor iff the thirteen stated linear constraints hold:\nsix null traces, six even-parity equalities, one cyclic odd-offdiagonal sum.\nTheir unique inverse gives symmetric trace-free mixed curvature B and\nLambda=-tr E. A supplied fixed Lambda adds tr E=-Lambda.\n\nTimelike-only rank6 misses five mixed components; null-only rank10 misses\nthe constant-curvature direction; combined rank11 reconstructs Q at that\npoint. Explicit bad-even and bad-odd records fail shared-tensor consistency.\nThis is necessary on each ACTUAL admitted Einstein development and sufficient\nonly for an algebraic curvature tensor. It is NOT arbitrary complete lawful\nCauchy-data/PDE realization, future metric determination or a device law.\nThe tidal convention is minus Jacobi relative acceleration. G335's pair\ndeformation is not substituted for this curvature tide. Frame, proper-time/\nruler calibration and affine normalization are ordinary query data.\n\nThe generic source-first21-variable bivector reconstruction independently\nimposed Bianchi/Einstein constraints, obtained the11-dimensional space and\n13-dimensional record annihilator, then checked the full candidate inverse.\nAuthor15 groups,11 exact basis tensors and four mutant failures are regression.\nOrbit-built symmetry checks alone do not prove the algebraic converse.\nThe guard named future/normalization checks null norm; future time component1\nand the supplied frame prove the stated eventwise normalization, not physical\ncalibration. The reviewer's F=-B translation is a slot convention, no defect.\nNo global/PDE/measurement/physical-content extension is banked.\n\n## G359 \u2014 SC4-JET, SC4-LOCAL, SC4-COMPACT\n\nControlling text: step_04/CANDIDATE_ARGUMENT.md, all sections.\nArgument SHA256:\n42f4c5881c9bf2f914b7682e50b030a30e50784fc9a671b2c77a2f427ff944ad.\nDirect review: step_04/review/STAGE_B_ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW.md, SHA256\n07180232e064e4c996792e3594d184274d841582d7409f8761ce57f6cb1611be.\nReview context /root/tri_step04_review; 0/1 post-review repairs.\n\nOn an ACTUAL supplied smooth time-oriented Lorentz metric, spacelike slice\nwith induced gamma/future unit normal n, and smooth REAL initial phase phi:\nnonzero future-null full initial covector requires and is given by\ndphi!=0, n(Theta)=-|dphi|_gamma,\nk|Sigma=dphi+|dphi|_gamma n-flat (spatial extension annihilates n).\nThe normal derivative is fixed by chosen spatial data and type, not another\nindependent free datum. Phi itself is not uniquely selected by the metric.\n\nAt each noncritical point, the fixed metric and phi determine a unique\nsmooth local future-null phase on a sufficiently small common characteristic\ngraph. Gaussian F=sqrt(gamma^ij p_i p_j), p!=0, gives Theta_t+F=0.\nThe characteristic/variational proof checks the FULL gradient and preserved\nnormalization, not merely tangential pullback or curve constancy.\nk# is affine geodesic; the Gaussian-time characteristic parameter need not be.\nNo uniform duration, global no-caustic theorem or PDE machine proof follows.\n\nOPTIONALLY demanding one smooth real nonzero null phase on a neighborhood of\nan entire nonempty compact boundary-free spacelike slice is impossible:\nan extremum of phi forces dphi=0 and hence k=0. This is NOT a G352 global\nrequirement, a refutation of compact metric developments, or adoption of a\ncircle-valued/atlas alternative. Local patches survive. No G356 harmonic-wave\nembedding into G321's compact family is claimed.\n\nLocal (theta,z) coordinates do not derive the CHOSEN phase-independent finite\nmeasure, spacing or cross-phase labels. Local free phase propagation is NOT\ncurvature-recipe/product persistence or physical content selection.\nAny G321/G335 application inherits imported development/smoothness limits.\n\nPreserve the pre-freeze structural symbolic-equality failure and diagnostic:\n(r-t)/r and 1-t/r differed structurally, with every exact difference zero.\nOnly equality testing changed; no equation, premise, tolerance or domain did.\nThe corrected18 guards and four mutant failures were exactly replayed.\nIndependent pre-exposure non-diagonal space/time-dependent metric and off-axis\nprojection controls passed18 checks. The critical-normal author guard only\nchecks a quadratic-form identity; analytic roots/compact extrema bear the\ntheorem, supplemented by reviewer real-root recomputation.\nThe reviewer discloses one read-only git-diff authentication despite the\ndispatch's shorthand no-git boundary; no repository mutation occurred.\n\n## G360 \u2014 SC5-ROBUST, SC5-CLASS, SC5-THRESHOLD\n\nControlling text: step_05/CANDIDATE_ARGUMENT.md, all sections, with the\ninitial direct review AND focused repair disposition (not initial PASS alone).\nArgument SHA256:\n50c7f90558bc623f227d5066a84a876017c563218f38426fd7e2f7a80fa5c7c9.\nInitial direct review: step_05/review/PHASE_B_ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW.md, SHA256\n8c38e95f920c88062dffae8f99311ce78cd15ad5edc743a28dffeb01225605ed.\nFocused review: step_05/repair/review/FOCUSED_REVIEW.md, SHA256\n4da1b276a75c6ca3501a9536c8ba0c8e2a68501a013aeff21106ee847493f9b8.\nContext /root/tri_step05_review, then the SAME exposed reviewer for focused\nrepair; 1/1 same-premise regression repair/review cycles consumed.\n\nRetain G357's exact three overlap windows, common finite nonnegative measure,\npositive reference rates, and supplied bounded measurable active weights\nf_i in [1-e,1+e], 0<=e<1. Then z_i=integral_Wi f_i dmu obeys z>=0 and\n(1-e)z_i <= (1+e)(z_j+z_k) for EVERY fixed allowed kernel triple.\nConversely those conditions suffice for SOME allowed kernels AND measure,\nnot every fixed kernel/observer/metric or pre-existing measure. A constant-\nweight smooth Minkowski subclass supplies the converse; arbitrary measurable\nweights are not asserted to have smooth observer realizations.\n\nFor nonzero z>=0 with S=sum z, the exact uncertainty-class threshold is\ne_*=max(0,2 max(z)/S-1). Zero is separate; one-positive records require\ne_*=1 and fail throughout the retained e<1 domain. For (1,1,3) the threshold\nis1/5 with exact boundary witness; fixed f_i=1 still fails at any nominal\nbound. No empirical20-percent accuracy is claimed. Finer measure/weights\nremain free; cell-mass uniqueness can be lost. Exact registration, absence\nof record noise and supported bounds are not smuggled in as established\ninstrument properties, population laws or additional physical premises.\n\nThe analytic pointwise dual inequalities and interval/triangle construction\nbear the quantifiers. Source-first different converse and six-ray exact\nfeasibility gave1542 assertions over1080 signed controls. Initial author1262\nassertions,625 controls,182 constructions/443 rejections and four mutant\nfailures did NOT certify all rejected classifications: the reviewer actually\nmade reject-ALL-nonzero return PASS377 with only5 zero constructions and620\nrejections. This false-pass evidence remains intact, not relabeled harmless.\n\nRepaired check_exact.py SHA256:\n7e0da03e320f6d53ef94f4b75afd816d7d0a2f25c242b837cc88f10d50cd9e2d.\nIts new per-record returned-status guard uses the reviewed feasibility\nthreshold; this is theorem-relative finite regression, NOT independent proof.\nActual1887 assertions/17 groups retain625 controls and182/443 disposition.\nAll five mutants fail, and the reviewer independently reapplied the ORIGINAL\nunconditional corruption, which now fails. Only docstring, mutation switch/\nbranch and status guard changed. Initial candidate/proof/code/reviews and\nall failed raw outputs stay frozen. No mathematical or physical repair occurred.\n\n## Review ceiling, promotion gates and preservation\n\nAll four original direct reviewers were actual fresh separate contexts with\nsource-first argument work. Exact runtime model UNKNOWN; different-model and\nhuman-specialist axes UNTESTED. Context, argument, implementation and model\nindependence are distinct. SC5 focused review is not a second blind context.\nShared capture infrastructure and author-code reruns are not independent\nscientific verification. Hashes prove correspondence, not truth or trusted\nchronology. No full reproof of all accepted inputs, actual observations,\ndetector calibration, generic PDE realization or physical adoption was done.\n\nThe fresh banking review is source/integration/proposal fidelity only.\nThe original scientific reviews remain controlling; omitted full old-suite\nreplays are disclosed, and old evidence is authenticated at its source pin.\nThe original339-row premise audit passed before any live registry/verifier\nedit (STARTUP_PREMISE_AUDIT.json). The clean343-row audit, startup regression/\nmutation checks, final fidelity disposition and actual commit/push outcome\nmust be recorded separately before claiming completed banking.\n\nThe fixed-snapshot manuscript and sidecar remain the through-G352/335-row\nedition at f23199e4a47aaf83acb9ea7d1ad382cd814159c2, not live343-row tracking.\nCANON.md and all prior campaign evidence remain unchanged. The46 original\nuntracked entries are preserved as metadata only; no protected payload read.\nBackup completeness and pre-reboot unsaved-state disposition remain UNVERIFIED.\nScratchDisk is unused and blocks archive-dependent tasks only.\n\n"
    },
    "udt_g357_g360_conditional_banking_2026-09-07/WORK_ORDER.md": {
      "sha256": "3fe175ce7d9ed21aa0c18dacbdff1d0d642ac575f33d5ab23ce88ed10841985d",
      "text": "# Authorized SC2--SC5 conditional mathematical banking\n\nDate: 2026-09-07 UTC. Synchronized baseline grok:\ned2f7432f068aa7a72628382b890596b3efba06a.\n\nCharles authorizes banking SC2--SC5 exactly at their reviewed conditional\nmathematical scopes through the existing promotion checks. SC1 remains a\nsource map. Preserve the complete original campaign, its repaired false-pass\nevidence, assumptions, chosen recipes and every review limitation. Update\ncurrent research tracking; do not rewrite historical pending/unpromoted text.\n\nQuestion: does the proposed G357--G360 integration faithfully preserve those\nfour reviewed results, and what bounded persistence campaign should Charles\nconsider next? This is source-preserving promotion and MAP/PONDER, not a new\nscientific construction or solve. No physical identification, counting law,\nrecipe adoption, scientific premise, canon or fixed-snapshot manuscript change.\nThe next campaign is a proposal only; no new campaign is authorized.\n\nWorkspace: this banking package, the exact premise registry and maintained\ncurrent tracking; minimal additive maintenance of the existing premise\nverifier and its startup tests required by four new rows. Preserve every\nexisting339 registry row byte-for-byte and every old evidence package.\nNo protected payload reads, archive/disk operations, worktree pruning or\nfurther infrastructure refactoring. Backup completeness and pre-reboot\nunsaved-state disposition remain UNVERIFIED. ScratchDisk blocks only\narchive-dependent tasks, none needed here.\n\nGates: authenticate source campaign at ed2f7432; report discovery/freeze/\nreview history and assumptions; clean original premise audit; fresh separate-\ncontext source-fidelity and integration review; actual relevant tests and\nmutation rejection; clean post-integration premise audit; preservation checks;\nscoped logical commit and push grok after all required gates pass.\nOld substantive scientific reviews supply scientific verification. New fidelity\nreview does not re-prove their mathematics or establish empirical truth.\n\nBudget: target90 minutes for this banking/decision return, CPU only. One full\npremise audit at a time, each2GiB address space and900 seconds CPU/wall;\nsmall check children512MiB/60 seconds. No scientific PDE solve or GPU.\nOne bounded source-preserving correction/focused fidelity re-review if needed.\nStop on unresolved load-bearing disagreement or permission/access/resource\nblocker; save a checkpoint if interrupted, do not claim banking completed.\n\nMaximum conclusion: BANKED_DERIVED_CONDITIONAL, VERIFIED-WITH-CAVEATS,\nowner-authorized mathematics only, and a source-grounded next-campaign\nproposal awaiting Charles's direction decision. All free data, optional\nconditions, CHOSEN recipes and physical exclusions remain explicit.\n\n"
    },
    "udt_g357_g360_conditional_banking_2026-09-07/NEXT_CAMPAIGN_PROPOSAL.md": {
      "sha256": "1c12a487694a942d09f85b44ed27235781005d8934c62884cbeee91e1640cfbf",
      "text": "# Proposed campaign \u2014 persistence of the chosen phase/current/product relation\n\nPROPOSAL ONLY, 2026-09-07 UTC. Awaiting Charles's direction decision.\nNo new campaign is authorized by the banking task.\n\n## Recommendation in plain language\n\nTest whether a chosen geometric construction that fits on an initial slice\ncontinues to fit when that same lawful metric develops. This could reveal a\nreal additional restriction on compatible initial data, a preserved subclass,\nor a failure of automatic preservation. It should not produce another special\ncompatibility example unless that example answers this different question.\n\nWe now have local existence for a freely supplied noncritical phase (G359)\nand a special-class criterion for matching a CHOSEN curvature current to a\nphase-independent product (G356). Neither says their relationship persists\non admitted metric developments. Conservation of the current is already\nknown NOT to imply the fixed-label product even within the harmonic class.\nRepeating that counterexample alone would not answer the new question.\n\nThe proposed target is conditional geometric compatibility, not photons,\nenergy, particles, physical counting or another familiar mechanism. A\nsuccessful persistence result would not identify physically carried content.\nFailure would not imply that a new physical premise is necessary.\n\n## What is already available, and what is not\n\nG312/G313 supplies the owner-provisional bounded Einstein arena Ric(g)=Lambda g.\nG321 conditionally applies the imported smooth Cauchy theorem to its registered\ncomplete compact marked T3 data; G332 supplies complete constraint data for its\nweighted-contact S3 family, and G335 inherits conditional local development\nthere. These are different admitted families, not interchangeable embeddings.\nG335's persistence of a nonzero pair-response sign is a continuity result,\nNOT preservation of a zero recipe residual, and its response q is NOT the\ncurvature-recurrence scalar below.\n\nG355/G356 concerns ACTUAL special harmonic metrics\ng=-2du dv+dx^2+dy^2+Hdu^2 with H_xx+H_yy=0. On their regular N>0 domain the\nCHOSEN Weyl/first-dual recipe has full tensor B=N du tensor4 and future root\nbeta=-N^(1/4)du. Its recurrence, the chosen scalar q_rec=g^-1(alpha,alpha),\nand D=q_rec beta# give a particular current. Those types and identities are\nnot yet supplied on arbitrary admitted developments. The campaign must test\ntheir domain, not silently define an unavailable root or recurrence.\n\nThe earlier full recipe is fixed, not redesigned. In its harmonic domain:\nnabla beta=alpha tensor beta, D=w partial_v, w=q_rec N^(1/4).\nG356's DIFFERENT phase is dTheta=-kappa(u)du. Its product criterion is\nw=kappa(u)s(z)/Delta, equivalently mixed derivatives of log w vanish for\nSOME aligned phase; an ALREADY FIXED phase further requires w/kappa to be\nindependent of u. These coordinates and fixed cross-phase labels belong to\nthat class; the criterion is not presumed valid verbatim in all geometries.\n\nSources: exact registry G312/G321/G332/G335/G351/G352 and G355/G356; the\ncontrolling G321, G332 and G335 AUDIT_REPORT.md files; G355/G356's unchanged\ncontent-bridge step_03/step_04 CANDIDATE_ARGUMENT.md; G359's unchanged\nshared-readout step_04 argument and review. BANKING_RECORD.md preserves grades.\nThe proposed work begins by reading each load-bearing controlling derivation,\nnot treating this proposal or a method checklist as scientific evidence.\n\n## Precise question and supplied versus imposed conditions\n\nSupply complete lawful metric data (Sigma,gamma,K and any fixed admitted\nsector/marking data), their actual conditional smooth development, a local\nreal spatial phase phi with dphi!=0, initial label registration, retained\npatch/support and positive spacing Delta. These are ordinary initial/query\ndata, free within their admitted conditions; they need not be uniquely chosen\nby the metric. G359 fixes n(Theta)=-|dphi|_gamma and locally extends Theta\nwhile its characteristic graph remains regular. That normal derivative is\nnot independently free once phi and the future-null type are fixed.\n\nHold the old curvature recipe fixed. Wherever its full root/recurrence\noperations actually exist, distinguish two already different routes:\n\n- ORIGINAL-ROOT phase: require dTheta=beta as a FULL ambient covector identity.\n  Within G355's harmonic class, closure of this root forces q_rec=0. Do not\n  require this same identity while claiming G356's positive q_rec route.\n- DIFFERENT-PHASE weighted current: beta need not be closed; require the\n  separately supplied/extended future-null k=dTheta to align with D, with\n  D=rho k# for an appropriate smooth positive rho on the retained domain.\n  The root remains beta, not a silently rescaled fourth root.\n\nFor the positive-current route, ask additionally whether the conserved current\nhas a well-defined ray-quotient intensity Xi that agrees with\n(|dTheta|/Delta) tensor mu for ONE phase-independent finite label measure\non the frozen labels. Any extension of the quotient construction beyond the\naccepted special class must itself be proved with its hypotheses, not inserted\nas a definition claiming equality. Product equality, finite/integrable measure,\ncurrent conservation and phase alignment are distinct conditions.\n\nIf mu is supplied independently, recipe equality is a compatibility restriction\non it. If mu is computed by requiring equality with a fixed smooth intensity,\nit is no longer an independently free second choice in that comparison.\nNeither case selects physical population. Relabeling across phases, changing\nthe initial phase or replacing the recipe during a fixed-input test changes\nthe test; it is not a repair of its original conclusion.\n\nThe central quantifier is: on an explicitly stated class of ACTUAL admitted\ndevelopments satisfying the recipe/domain and full compatibility conditions\ninitially, do those conditions hold on some nonzero local interval?\nAn initial residual R|Sigma=0 is not a proof that R=0 nearby.\nA computed nonzero normal derivative of a required residual on a complete\nlawful compatible datum could disprove automatic preservation; vanishing\nfinitely many derivatives cannot prove general smooth preservation.\nFor a positive result, derive a propagation argument from admitted evolution\nand the stated initial conditions, or prove a genuinely invariant subclass.\nThese are proposed methods and outcome criteria, not new results asserted here.\n\n## Adaptive scope \u2014 at most three substantive reviewed steps\n\n1. **Domain and admissible-data gate.** Specify the unchanged recipe, each\n   operation's nonzero/type/regularity domain, exact initial residuals and\n   the admitted Cauchy-data interface. Determine whether the proposed initial\n   compatibility class is supported and which data it restricts. Distinguish\n   algebraic pointwise compatibility from complete lawful data and a developed\n   spacetime. Do not assume special harmonic null-u cuts are spacelike Cauchy\n   slices or that their metrics embed in G321's compact family.\n   Outcomes: a usable conditional class; a scoped incompatibility/obstruction;\n   or an unsupported join that must remain open.\n\n2. **First loss or a propagation identity.** On the surviving class, use\n   admitted metric evolution to examine the first unconstrained derivative\n   of alignment/root/product defects. Seek either a lawful initially compatible\n   counterexample with rigorously nonzero departure, or a closed propagation\n   argument. Special solutions count only as controls or as a rigorously\n   identified subclass, not evidence for generic preservation.\n   A recurrence/type-domain loss and a product mismatch are different failures.\n\n3. **Only if informative: boundary of the surviving result.** Check whether an\n   identified extra compatibility condition is preserved or just delays failure,\n   or establish the exact freedom left by a reviewed preservation result.\n   Include a distinguishable compatible/failed control only where it tests that\n   new boundary. Do not invent a third task after an adequate negative answer.\n\nBefore each step record question, quantifier/regime, assumptions, free data,\nrecipe-imposed restrictions, methods/controls, omissions, possible outcomes\nand maximum conclusion. A condition may be studied as an explicitly conditional\nmathematical restriction without adopting it as an additional physical law.\nStop if continuing would actually require a new physical commitment.\n\n## Budget, review and stopping conditions\n\nProposed authorization: at most3 substantive reviewed steps OR4 hours elapsed,\nwhichever comes first, including construction, checks, fresh separate-context\nsource-first adversarial review, and at most1 same-premise repair/focused\nre-review per step. Stop earlier if no useful in-scope continuation remains.\nNo routine task-by-task reauthorization within the approved campaign.\nA reviewed provisional result may support conditional downstream work only\nwith all assumptions and caveats carried forward.\n\nRepository-only analytic/exact-CPU work; no metric PDE production solve or GPU.\nSmall checks: one child per context,512MiB/60 seconds CPU/wall; full standard\npremise audits sequentially2GiB/900 seconds where required. No external archive\nor protected payload, disk operation or infrastructure overhaul. More resources\nor production computation requires separate authority. Keep one compact log,\nfreeze candidates before review findings, preserve failures/commands/manifests,\nand commit/push scoped candidate/review evidence under existing grok rules.\nIf interrupted, save a resumable checkpoint and do not claim completion.\n\nStop for a necessary new physical commitment, unresolved load-bearing review\ndisagreement after the one repair, unavailable required development/domain\nhypothesis with no useful conditional continuation, permission/access/safety/\nresource blocker, lack of a useful distinct question, or the budget limit.\nReturn reviewed conditional results and a decision brief, not automatic\nscientific promotion. No accepted grade, manuscript, premise or canon change.\n\n## What the alternatives would establish\n\nA positive general propagation result would make initial compatibility\nsufficient on its proved local class: an additional connection between the\nadmitted metric evolution and this chosen construction. A narrower positive\nresult would identify a compatible invariant subclass, with its remaining\ninitial data and optional restrictions stated explicitly. Neither selects\nthat subclass as the physically occupied one or derives a counting law.\n\nA lawful initially compatible departure would refute automatic preservation\nfor this fixed recipe/relationship and stated class, and isolate the failed\ncondition. It would not refute UDT, all G352 realizations, free local phases\nor all metric-derived constructions. Failure of recipe admissibility already\non the initial slice would instead limit the candidate's domain; it would\nnot be a dynamic counterexample. An unresolved interface means OPEN, not\nnonexistence or evidence that a new premise must be adopted.\n\nCharles's next decision: authorize this bounded persistence campaign as scoped,\nnarrow its admitted-data/route target, or choose another direction. The current\nbanking authorization alone does not make that choice.\n\n"
    }
